# ─── Retired Astro starter posts (indexed at launch, removed in 078dd39) ───
# These have no page. Without explicit rules they 404; previously the blanket
# trailing-slash rule below re-matched its own output and looped infinitely.
/blog/first-post            /blog/  301
/blog/first-post/           /blog/  301
/blog/second-post           /blog/  301
/blog/second-post/          /blog/  301
/blog/third-post            /blog/  301
/blog/third-post/           /blog/  301
/blog/markdown-style-guide  /blog/  301
/blog/markdown-style-guide/ /blog/  301
/blog/using-mdx             /blog/  301
/blog/using-mdx/            /blog/  301

# NOTE: the rule `/blog/:slug  /blog/:slug/  301` was removed deliberately.
# It was redundant for real pages (Netlify Pretty URLs already appends the
# trailing slash for directories that exist) and for any slug WITHOUT a page
# it redirected to a target that re-matched the same rule, producing an
# infinite loop. Missing slugs must 404 cleanly instead.

# ─── Host canonicalization: http → https, www → apex ───
http://multiplycmo.com/*       https://multiplycmo.com/:splat  301!
http://www.multiplycmo.com/*   https://multiplycmo.com/:splat  301!
https://www.multiplycmo.com/*  https://multiplycmo.com/:splat  301!
